nt Shomari Figures (D) is running."]}, "overview": "First-term Democrat Shomari Figures defends a newly drawn Alabama district that leans Republican by seven points, facing Rhett Marques in a race most forecasters expect to flip. Polling from Democratic sponsors has shown the race tied since midsummer, and headlines emphasize Republican worries about turnout, prompting a Trump rally in Mobile in early October.\n\nMarques benefits from roughly $2.9 million in outside support and NFIB backing, while Figures holds a cash-on-hand edge. Prediction markets price the Democrat near 30 percent. The combination of district lean, environment, and outside spending gives the Republican a modest but real advantage, with enough polling uncertainty to keep the race within reach.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2955, "margin": -3.05}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2762, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3161, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3129, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2478, "margin": -4.0}]}